<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico assigns first two auctions.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico assigns first two auctions.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico assigned the first two of seven auctions whereby it sought to drain 5.797 billion pesos from the secondary market on Tuesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The auctions were offered or assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM     AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>600 million  31 days  25.49 pct</p>
<p>600 million  30 days  25.40 pct</p>
<p>600 million  27 days</p>
<p>1.400 bln  20 days</p>
<p>    1.300 bln   9 days</p>
<p>	600 million   3 days</p>
<p>	697 million   1 day</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>((-- Mexico City newsroom 525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
